      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Understood; updating the assessment. The 45-second telemetry drop could indeed indicate a localized technical disruption, possibly a jamming attempt rather than hostile interference. However, there is a 20% chance this could be an intelligence breach signal. If this were a hostile action, we could see an attempt to mislead regarding the extraction squad's position. The asset has been algorithmically shielded, and this should safeguard against simplistic jamming techniques.\n\nGiven that a localized jam could also denote a fiendish safeguard measure around the asset, we would require a surgical extraction approach. Otherwise, the mission's integrity and asset security remain solid. I advise bolstering our communication redundancy and deploying a rapid response team to verify and counter any such interference while evacuation remains on schedule. Please confirm if you wish to delay extraction or implement these extra precautions.",
